  "raw": " get its many glitches fixed, photos from China purportedly show an exposed Pixel 3 XL booting up and demonstrating the number one resource — battery life — in Google's latest phone.\n\nWhich isn't good news for those hoping the P3XL will help improve Google's often dreary software support and buggy devices.\n\nGoogle said early this year that it had removed some of its more undesirable features such as USB type-C connectivity and a notch on the front to hide the selfie camera. But my review unit boasted both a notch display and major bugs. If my experience is typical, then we're not buying the $999 Pixel 3 until some Big G comes up with a fix for unspecified bugs. The screen not responding at boot up being just one example.\n\nThese bad daylight arrivals are all reportedly coming through faulty materials. The information comes via a thread expired Monday evening on Chinese social media service Weibo, according to PCMag editor-in-chief Sascha Segan.\n",
  "serialized": "get its many glitches fixed, photos from China purportedly show an exposed Pixel 3 XL booting up and demonstrating the number one resource — battery life — in Google's latest phone. Which isn't good news for those hoping the P3XL will help improve Google's often dreary software support and buggy devices. Google said early this year that it had removed some of its more undesirable features such as USB type-C connectivity and a notch on the front to hide the selfie camera. But my review unit boasted both a notch display and major bugs. If my experience is typical, then we're not buying the $999 Pixel 3 until some Big G comes up with a fix for unspecified bugs. The screen not responding at boot up being just one example. These bad daylight arrivals are all reportedly coming through faulty materials. The information comes via a thread expired Monday evening on Chinese social media service Weibo, according to PCMag editor-in-chief Sascha Segan.",
